Local patch for the BLUETTI custom integration on vesta (card #319, runbook
bluetti-selfheal.md §2e). NOT applied by anything in this repo: an owner step.

Against: bluetti-official/bluetti-home-assistant v1.0.5 (commit f1df72b),
         custom_components/bluetti/models.py
         sha256 before c8f10ea078d23312c4ebf905970977bb63ea1f516e61e4d1827207a5ff36cbf4
         sha256 after  cfe58a38d83cf730a66c532ddd5de05b26cc40cb10f0175bc39d58c0486f86d6
Why:     the cloud sends the device serial as data.deviceSn; v1.0.3–v1.0.5 read
         only data.message.deviceSn, so every websocket push raises
         KeyError('message'), which the listener swallows — and in cloud mode
         nothing else refreshes the entities (upstream #171, #172, #176).
Apply:   patch -p3 models.py < this file   (on a copy; then put it on vesta and
         RESTART Home Assistant — an integration reload keeps the old module)
Lost on: any HACS update / redownload of the integration.
         binary_sensor.bluetti_push_dead (bluetti_selfheal >= 1.2.0) notices.

--- a/custom_components/bluetti/models.py
+++ b/custom_components/bluetti/models.py
@@ -63,7 +63,17 @@
 
         res = json.loads(message)
         # load api
-        sn = res["data"]["message"]["deviceSn"]
+        # home-assitant card #319 (upstream #171 / #172 / #176): the cloud sends the
+        # serial as data.deviceSn OR as data.message.deviceSn. Accept both; a frame
+        # with neither is ignored instead of raising (the KeyError was swallowed by
+        # StompListener.__callback and no refresh was ever scheduled).
+        data = res.get("data") if isinstance(res, dict) else None
+        data = data if isinstance(data, dict) else {}
+        nested = data.get("message")
+        sn = (nested.get("deviceSn") if isinstance(nested, dict) else None) or data.get("deviceSn")
+        if not sn:
+            __LOGGER__.debug("ws message without a deviceSn, ignored")
+            return
 
         device = self.get_device_by_sn(sn)
         if device and device.control_mode != ControlMode.BLE:
